load ../credential-scope-narrowing.maude

--- Fixture discipline: every fixture carries an attempt against BOTH a
--- listed and an unlisted target where relevant, so what separates admitted
--- from refused is the grant's class discipline, never the absence of an
--- attempt the author could have made.

--- Coverage: the narrowable happy path. A request grant with its list admits
--- a listed target.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-SCOPE-NARROWING :
  grantList(h1, reqOp) listed(h1, reqOp, tIn) attempt(h1, reqOp, tIn)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(h1, reqOp, tIn) .

--- Coverage: the non-narrowable happy path. A bare sign grant admits sign.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-SCOPE-NARROWING :
  grantBare(h1, signOp) attempt(h1, signOp, tIn)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(h1, signOp, tIn) .

--- Coverage: a glob list on `sign` is a CHECK ERROR, not a silent no-op.
--- Section 14: silent acceptance is precisely the over-promise avoided.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-SCOPE-NARROWING :
  grantList(h1, signOp)
  =>* C:Cfg checkError .

--- Coverage: a bare `request` grant is a CHECK ERROR -- the narrowable class
--- REQUIRES its list.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-SCOPE-NARROWING :
  grantBare(h1, reqOp)
  =>* C:Cfg checkError .

--- Coverage: the negative fixture. Under the rejected uniform-glob design,
--- a request to a target OUTSIDE the grant's list is admitted anyway -- the
--- clause read as narrowed and meant nothing. This Solution is what gives
--- the No-solutions below their bite.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-SCOPE-NARROWING-UNIFORM :
  grantList(h1, reqOp) listed(h1, reqOp, tIn) attempt(h1, reqOp, tOut)
  =>* C:Cfg admitted(h1, reqOp, tOut) .

--- THE NARROWING. In the real design, a request outside the list is never
--- admitted -- even with the grant present, the list populated, and the
--- attempt made. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-SCOPE-NARROWING :
  grantList(h1, reqOp) listed(h1, reqOp, tIn) attempt(h1, reqOp, tOut)
  =>* admitted(h1, reqOp, tOut) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- A glob-list grant on `sign` grants NOTHING: the sign attempt is refused
--- even though the clause names its operation -- the malformed shape errors
--- instead of quietly authorizing. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-SCOPE-NARROWING :
  grantList(h1, signOp) listed(h1, signOp, tIn) attempt(h1, signOp, tIn)
  =>* admitted(h1, signOp, tIn) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- No grant, no admission -- for either class. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-SCOPE-NARROWING :
  attempt(h1, reqOp, tIn) attempt(h1, signOp, tIn)
  =>* admitted(H:Hnd, O:Op, T:Tgt) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- The well-formed grant pair -- listed request, bare sign -- raises no
--- check error: the class discipline rejects only the malformed shapes.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-SCOPE-NARROWING :
  grantList(h1, reqOp) listed(h1, reqOp, tIn) grantBare(h1, signOp)
  =>* checkError RESIDUAL:Cfg .
